metro officers from the bolton area  command swarmed liberty baptist church  this morning but it wasn't for an  emergency  the call went far beyond that to prevent  crime from happening in the first place  hector mejia joins us live near lake  mead and rainbow to explain hi hector  hey there usually when you see a cluster  of cop cars you automatically think  something bad happened and you start to  worry  this time was different though officers  went straight into the kitchen  and made pancakes for people to enjoy  the event pastors police and pancakes  brought a few dozen people from  different denominations out to liberty  baptist church this morning  it's the first time such a large group  of pastors and metro police officers  were able to reconnect  during the pandemic the efforts go back  several years though as part of the  police department's recap program  rebuilding every city around peace the  goal has been to prevent violence and  reduce tensions in the community we're  told it's proven to be successful  we've seen lives changed we've seen  hungry kids find  help we've seen kids who need shoes fine  shoes we've seen kids who are  academically struggling find peer  counselors or mentors  an event like this it warms your heart  makes you feel good inside when you have  people that come out  and support you and support the efforts  and they want to come around you to  reduce the violence  a few years after this program was  launched in this community alone  violent crime dropped 75 percent that  was between 2013  and 2014 calls for service also dropped  27 percent  the bouldin area command covers 17.3  square miles and according to captain  carlos hank  right now communities all across the u.s  are craving peace  especially after everything we've been  dealing with over the last year  hector mejia reporting 8 news now
 

